	(text "UVLO divider R1/R2: on at ~9.0 V, off at ~7.3 V.\nFeedback R3/R4 (118k / 22.1k): 5.07 V out."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.11 78.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "07c545f2-58a9-55ce-a93e-0ba91b9a2eed")
	)
	(text "USB OUTPUT  (TPS2553 current-limited switch, ~117 mA)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "22c19029-9a1d-523b-91ab-644d8a0ac6c5")
	)
	(text "From the ESP32 board's J2 (TAB_OUT, ~16 V, current-limited to\n~87 mA there by limiter 2).\n\nD1 SMBJ24A sits before D2: if the cable is wired backwards D1\nconducts, limiter 2 holds the current and the firmware switches\nthe output off. D2 SS16 blocks reverse current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6dfc1918-b67c-5554-b7c5-630c926e159b")
	)
	(text "INPUT PROTECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 31.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2db96bf-039a-52ec-bbfe-4b43c9161ac6")
	)
	(text "5 V BUCK  (LMR51606, 1.1 MHz PFM)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 31.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e30a4166-b303-530e-80ca-95f70b31860d")
	)
	(text "R5 232k sets the limit to ~117 mA typ. The TPS2553 (not the -1\nversion) holds a constant current in overload rather than latching\noff, so a tablet asking for 1-2 A just sees VBUS sag.\n\nJP1 open (default): D+/D- left open, a basic USB port.\nClose JP1 to short D+/D- (\"dedicated charger\") if the tablet\ncharges better that way. The current limit is the same.\n\nUse a normal USB-A to USB-C cable to the tablet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 182.88 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e3d1e469-96a6-5e38-8c7d-ce69da08d1a1")
	)
